    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a no-show cancellation-fee dispute on trip TRP-00853. The rider filed it, contesting the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee. On the evidence, the fee stands and the driver is entitled to compensation.\n\nWhy the fee stands. The driver pressed 'arrived' at 18:10:00 at the Tampines MRT pickup, which the trip record classes as a TRANSPORT_HUB (arrival radius 150 m). The GPS trace EV-GPS-00853 places him at the pin itself — maximum, mean and minimum distance 0.0 m — stationary at 0 kph from 18:10:00 to 18:14:00, a single continuous in-geofence dwell of 240 seconds. The free waiting period in force is 180 seconds (EV-TRIP-00853, platform_policy.free_wait_sec), and no_show_threshold_sec is null. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold: (a) the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event; (b) the trace places the driver inside the geofence at that timestamp; (c) he held position for 240 seconds against a 180-second minimum, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix; and (d) the driver terminated the trip at 18:14:00 — after the dwell elapsed at 18:13:00 — with no boarding event and the recognised reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 (he was 0 m from the pin at 0 kph, nowhere near 300 m or 15 kph). POL-NS-03, the wrong-entrance clause, does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not merely within 400 m of it. POL-NS-06 gives no refund because the dwell was a surplus, not a shortfall, against the minimum.\n\nThe rider's message. At 18:10:20 the rider sent the only message on the trip: 'I am by the pickup pin and cannot see you. Where are you?' That is a locating and coordinating message, and the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed any in-app call (in_app_calls is empty), so POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) hold. But limb (c) cannot be run: the trace carries no rider track at all (derived.rider_presence.available is false). Under POL-NS-11 the limb is UNDECIDABLE — neither satisfied nor failed — so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider, and the fee is decided on the driver's own evidence. I have not inferred from the silence of the rider track that the rider was elsewhere, and per POL-NS-11 that missing track does not impair the driver's arrival or dwell evidence, does not engage POL-NS-08(b) or POL-NS-09(e), and does not lower the confidence cap on a finding resting on the driver's track.\n\nImpaired artifact. The only impaired artifact is EV-ADVIS-00853-01 (traffic advisory), MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. Nobody relies on it: it could only bear on POL-NS-06 limb (i), which permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only where a populated advisory exists — and here the dwell was one continuous 240-second run, so limb (i) is not engaged. Its absence is citable but shortens, extends and excuses nothing.\n\nMoney and outcome. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is paid 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee = SGD 3.60, the exact figure the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00853) computes. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/100 = 0.01 (below 0.08), so no compensation is withheld and nothing escalates. No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is present — there is no contradiction between artifacts on arrival, dwell or rider presence; both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0; no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and the deciding facts rest on COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and my confidence is 0.9. Under POL-GEN-03 the rider's charge of SGD 4.50 is left standing (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) and the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, where amount_sgd carries the same figure as driver_compensation_sgd, SGD 3.60. The monetary effect of SGD 3.60 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05. No clause in this record produces a referral."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

