    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute concerns the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-00853 (EV-FARE-00853: cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED). The rider asks for it back; it stands.\n\nTHE CHARGE IS VALID UNDER POL-NS-01. All four limbs hold on this record. (a) The trip record (EV-TRIP-00853) contains a driver 'arrived' event at 18:10:00. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00853) places the driver 0.0 m from the pickup pin at that same timestamp, well inside the TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius of 150 m (POL-NS-02), and POL-NS-02's consecutive-fix test is met 25 times over. (c) The driver held position at 0.0 m for a single continuous in-geofence run of 240 seconds, from 18:10:00 to 18:14:00, against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec); no longer threshold applies because no_show_threshold_sec is null. (d) The trip record records no boarding event and a driver termination at 18:14:00 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one minute after the required dwell elapsed at 18:13:00.\n\nPOL-NS-05 does not bite and produces no referral: at 18:10:00 the driver was stationary at the pin at a recorded 0 kph, so the arrival marker is TRUE and the waiting clock runs from the arrival event itself.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CONTACT DOES NOT EXONERATE. The rider's message at 18:10:20 ('I am by the pickup pin and cannot see you. Where are you?') satisfies POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b): it is locating in content, and the driver neither replied in the chat within 120 seconds nor placed any in-app call before terminating. But limb (c) requires the rider's own track to place the rider's device within 200 m of the pin for the majority of qualifying fixes, and the trace carries no rider track at all (rider_presence.available is false). Under POL-NS-11 that makes limb (c) UNDECIDABLE, not failed: POL-NS-04 cannot by itself exonerate the rider, and the missing rider track does not impair the driver's arrival or dwell evidence, does not engage POL-NS-08(b) or POL-NS-09(e), and does not lower the confidence cap on a finding that rests on the driver's track. The dispute is therefore decided on the driver's evidence under POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-07. I record both advocates' agreement on this point.\n\nWEIGHT AND INTEGRITY. The artifacts carrying the deciding facts are EV-TRIP-00853 and EV-GPS-00853, both at weight 1.0. The arrival event timestamp matches the nearest GPS fix exactly (no clock skew), the trace holds 25 fixes at a 10-second cadence with no gap over 120 seconds and no gap straddling the cancellation, the chat log's 1 message equals trip_record.chat_message_count of 1 with no redaction, and the 4.50 charged reconciles with the net figure produced by the resolution rule. The single impaired artifact, EV-ADVIS-00853-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no deciding fact here, because the dwell was one continuous run and no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) was needed; it therefore does not cap confidence and its absence is not relied on by the driver. No POL-NS-03 mislocation arises (the driver was inside the radius, at the pin).\n\nOUTCOME. The rider's claim to have the charge returned is not supported, and the charge stands as it presently is. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the 4.50 fee = 3.60 SGD, the figure the fare breakdown itself computes. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below the 4 threshold) and the ratio to 100 completed trips in 30 days is 0.01 (below 0.08). No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is present: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the artifacts do not contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, neither profile shows counterparty disputes in the last 90 days (both 0), rider no-show disputes in 30 days is 0, and the sole impaired artifact is not the evidence for any deciding fact. The profile fields cited (no_show_terminations_30d, completed_trips_30d) are the ones POL-NS-07 names; the lifetime counters are treated as context only, per POL-GEN-01. The ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and per POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries the same 3.60 figure because that is the amount the ruling moves; the rider's own charge stands. The monetary effect (3.60) does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of 8.00, so it executes automatically on issue, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
